<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugo July industry output up 0.9 pct, 6.7 pct y/y.</title>
<headline>Yugo July industry output up 0.9 pct, 6.7 pct y/y.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT    JUNE	   MAY    JUNE 96</p>
<p> pct change mth/mth	     + 0.9	 - 2.4     + 2.9</p>
<p> pct change yr/yr		 + 6.7	 + 9.3     + 1.2</p>
<p> index (base average 1996)    103.9	 103.0     + 2.6</p>
<p>CUMULATIVE DATA (JAN TO JUNE)</p>
<p> pct change yr/yr		 + 7.6	 + 8.0     +  2.1</p>
<p>SEASONALLY ADJUSTED DATA</p>
<p> index (base average 1996)    103.2	 102.5	102.1</p>
<p>NOTES -- June industry output was 51.9-percent lower than in the same month 1991, before the breakup of former Yugoslavia.</p>
<p>Cumulative January-June output was 54.2 percent below output in the same six-month period 1991.</p>
<p>Data largely exclude private sector, where manufacturing is not significant. Data cover Federal Republic of Yugoslavia, comprising Serbia and Montenegro.</p>
<p>-- Amra Kevic, Belgrade newsroom +381 11 311 4305</p>
